 2 Types
 
 1. compile time/static polymorphism
 --------------------
 Binding of method declaration with method definition occurs compile time
 example : constr method overloading
 
 
 2. runtime/dynamic polymorphism
  Binding of method declaration with method definition occurs run time
 example: method overriding.
 
 Overriding
 -----------
 
 changin parents class non static methods implementation inside the child class is called overriding
 
 Rules
 
 1. name and params must be same
 2. wrt access modifiers while overriding a method visibility can be increased or kept same but cannot be decresed
 
 Parent  :   public     protected           default                   private
 
 Child   :   public     protected/public   default/protected/public   cannot be overriden cause its not inherited
 
 3.  wrt return type
 
 primitive->     void + int float    Cannot change
 
 non primtive -> Co variant types allowed to change
                 contra variant types are not allowed
 
 4. wrt final
 ------------------
          -> variable => variable cannot be re assigned   (they are inherited)
    final -> method   => cannot be overriden               (they are inherited)
          -> class   =>  cannot have child class
 
 5. wrt static
 
    static methods canot be overriden because they are not diff for diff instances of the same class
    althouh it looks like overriding its not its called method hiding.
 
 6. wrt abstract
 
 abstract can be overridden as concrete and concrete can be overidden as abstarct
 
 
 
 
 Accessmodifiers wrt vars and methods
 ---------------------------------------
 
 private - > any member marked as private its accessible only inside the class its declared in
 default - > any member left default is accessible only inside the package its declared in
 protected -> same as default + but can be accesed outside the package by inheriting its constituent class
 public -> access throught the project by importing
 
 
 Note: for a class only Public and default are allowed (unless its inner class)
 
